#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
UFO SHOOTER - a tkinter arcade game (menu + leaderboard edition).

Controls
  Move gun ........ Mouse  or  Left/Right (A/D)
  Shoot ........... Hold Left Mouse Button  or  hold SPACE
  Missile ......... T : fires a homing missile at the nearest UFO (4 s cooldown)
  Charge beam ..... Hold V to charge an energy ball, release V to fire a laser.
                    Held 2 s = SMALL (cyan), 3 s = MEDIUM (magenta),
                    4 s = LARGE (orange). Bigger charge = wider, harder beam.
                    Let go before 2 s and the charge fizzles out.
                    You can't use the normal gun while charging.
  Ricochet burst .. B : fires a fan of 5 bullets (one per direction) that bounce
                    off the edges of the screen 5 times before they vanish
                    (6 s cooldown). Tune BOUNCE_* near the top of the script.
  Minions ......... M : summons 2 mini guns on each side of your gun for 20 s.
                    They follow you, shoot bullets, and fire a homing missile
                    every 5 s - but only while an enemy is on screen.
                    (35 s cooldown; tune MINION_* near the top of the script.)
  Elements ........ 1 Frost, 2 Thunder, 3 Fire, 4 Poison (during a run).
                    Frost + Poison and Thunder + Fire can be combined.
                    An element imbues EVERYTHING you shoot for 15 s (30 s
                    cooldown each; incompatible pairs cannot be combined):
                      Frost   - hit UFOs are slowed for 3 s
                      Thunder - hit UFOs are stunned (bosses only briefly)
                      Fire    - bullets (and missiles / shockwaves) travel faster
                      Poison  - hit UFOs take damage over time for 3 s
                    Combos happen automatically: with an element active,
                    Charge beam / Shockwave (S) / Missiles (T) become the
                    elemental version (Frost Charge, Fire Shockwave, ...).
                    Tune ELEMENT_* / FROST_* / THUNDER_* / FIRE_* / POISON_*
                    near the ELEMENTAL ABILITIES block at the bottom.
  Pause ........... P
  Quit run ........ click QUIT RUN during play, in the shop, or while paused;
                    the partial run is saved and its summary is shown
  Shop............ click an upgrade, or press 1-8;  ENTER / SPACE = next wave
  Home menu ....... click PLAY / LEADERBOARD  (or press ENTER / L)
    Play ............ choose NORMAL (ends at wave 100), INFINITY, or ADAPTIVE
  Difficulty ...... choose Easy, Normal, Hard, or Nightmare before a run
  Tutorial ......... first run guide (skippable; replay it in Options)
  Options .......... O on the home screen: rebind controls, adjust volume,
                    reduce shake/flashes, enlarge HUD text, or enable
                    high-contrast warnings
  Objectives ....... click the objective panel or press O to collapse it
  Wave briefing .... every 3 waves choose a 3-wave bonus, upgraded through
                    three tiers by repeating it; every 5 waves choose an
                    optional risk/reward modifier (ESC skips)
  Leaderboard ..... mouse wheel or Up/Down to scroll, ESC to go back
  Game over ....... R = play again, M = main menu, L = leaderboard, TAB = stats
  Victory ......... R = play again, M = main menu, L = leaderboard, TAB = stats
  Fullscreen ...... F or F11 to toggle  (ESC also leaves fullscreen)
  Badges .......... click BADGES (or press B) to see your achievements
  Quests .......... click QUESTS (or press Q) for daily/weekly gem rewards
  Pets ............ click PETS (or press P) to hatch/equip pets; combine 3
                    identical pets into a Huge pet with a bonus buff
  UFO Index ....... click INDEX (or press I) to view encountered UFOs
  Skins ........... click SKINS (or press K): spend gems on bullet, gun and
                    missile skins. Switch tabs with the mouse or Left/Right/Tab,
                    scroll with the wheel or Up/Down, pick a row with 1-7.
                    You earn gems when a run ends: score / 100, rounded.
  Sound ........... S (or the SOUND button on the menu) toggles sound effects.
                    They are generated in code - no audio files needed. For the
                    best result (many sounds layered at once): pip install pygame

Every finished run (score, wave reached, rank and date), your unlocked badges,
quest progress and lifetime stats are saved to ufo_leaderboard.json next to this
script (or in ~/.ufo_shooter/ if the script's folder isn't writable). Your
progress is also checkpointed after every wave, so even if the game is killed
mid-run (IDE stop button, crash, power loss) that run is recovered on the next
launch.
"""

